"""Full-text appraisal, batch 34 (2026-11-22, late night): roadmap step 1c, papers Brendan fetched on his own access.

He sent 16 files (9 PDFs, 7 saved web pages). Read here: 14. Two had no body text:
  mackillop-2026  saved Taylor & Francis page shows the abstract only (no access); stays in the queue.
  petersen-1956   saved Wiley page shows only the first-page preview image (OCR'd): the psychosis began at a
                  tuberculosis sanatorium in spring 1954, about five months before the air embolism, with
                  confusion and agitation; the outcome is on the pages not seen. Stays in the queue.

Coded (11): spiers-2016, nguyen-2021, feldinger-2013, hefzy-2011, taira-2003, leonard-rapoport-1987,
godschalx-dekker-2014, yeung-2020, zuschlag-2016, rosenblat-2013, klok-2025.
Excluded (3):
  choo-2024          E1: a mild manic relapse (Young Mania 11, much milder than her usual 22) on full maintenance
                     treatment, remitting within 15 days of admission; an acute episode, the kind criterion 1 leaves out
                     (as with graham-2018 and arora-2006).
  de-santis-1997     E4: the authors present the psychosis as an expression of untreated coeliac disease, and it cleared
                     on a gluten-free diet: the calibration rule T3 (v1.8.6), psychosis attributed to coeliac disease.
  puente-1985        E3: the author hypothesised in advance that taking part in the research would reduce the
                     patient's symptoms, so the exposure was framed as therapy (dual intent, rule T1).
Run from the repo root:  python3 scripts/batches/b2026_11_22_appraisal_b34.py
"""
import sys

sys.path.insert(0, "scripts")
from lib_code import Batch, ev, track, T, A, J, N, H  # noqa: E402

b = Batch("2026-11-22", source="Full text supplied by Brendan")
S = lambda scale, v: [{"scale": scale, "value": v}]  # noqa: E731

